  "summary": "Bundled SDK with generic HTTP POST patterns; no traced installer harm",
  "details": "The package is an SDK distributed as a minified/bundled dist/index.js. Pattern matching flagged multiple POST call sites and a token 'dyndns' in the bundle, but these are keyword co-occurrences within a large minified bundle typical of SDKs (HTTP client code paths and string tables). No hardcoded attacker-controlled destination is bound to installer-side secret reads, no lifecycle install/postinstall hooks execute network fetches, and no import-time exfiltration path is present. The behavior observed is consistent with a normal SDK exposing HTTP client methods, not an installer-side attack.",
